@startuml
'https://plantuml.com/sequence-diagram

note left of Paperly
  It's presumed that Paperly handles logic for when to
  generate notifications, and for whom.
end note

[-> Paperly : send notification request

group oAuth client credentials grant
    Paperly -> Schoolbox : send request with client ID + secret
    Schoolbox -> Paperly : sends access token
end

note right of Paperly
  Paperly does not know the internal ID of Schoolbox users:
  only their SIS ID and role type.

  This means that Schoolbox will need an endpoint for sending
  notifications to a user based on their SIS ID + role type:
  currently the caller must know the user's internal ID.
end note

Paperly -> Schoolbox : sends request to send notification, with access token as authorization
Schoolbox ->]: sends notification via configured channels
note right of Schoolbox
  Schoolbox knows a user's notification preferences,
  and can forward them appropriately.
end note

@enduml
